        {
          "id": "SP_ISABELLA_MIRABILIS_SCHLACHER_HOENLINGER_PISERA_HOOPER_2005",
          "name": "Isabella mirabilis Schlacher-Hoenlinger, Pisera & Hooper, 2005",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Isabella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Growth Form. Massive ficiform or egg cup shaped sponge with a shallow apical dish, a short broad based stem and an uneven margin (Figs 1, 2); outer surface bearing numerous, short (up to 1 cm), unevenly distributed wart like buds (Fig. 3). Dimensions are 3 – 7.5 cm long, 2.5 – 7 cm wide and 3 – 5 cm high. Several specimens have a roughly circular base which is approximately 1 cm less in diameter than the body. Colour. Wine Dark purple / brown in ethanol. Oscules. Numerous microscopic exhalant oscules 0.05 – 0.2 mm in diameter. Texture. Hard, slightly compressible but brittle. Surface ornamentation. Uneven and slightly hispid caused by oxeas protruding several millimetres above the surface. Ectosomal skeleton. The ectosomal skeleton consists of an exterior skin like crust of microscleres with smooth dichotriaenes and occasionally triaenes perpendicular to the surface. The microscleres consist of abundant asymmetrical euasters like streptasters resembling jacks, and microxeas. The microxeas consist of smooth and microspinose curved oxeas that are predominantly centrotylote. Choanosomal skeleton. The choanosomal skeleton consists of a 3 D matrix of regular and slightly curved dicranoclone desmas. These desmas form a distinct root / vine like mesh (as described in Schlacher-Hoenlinger et al. 2005). Choanosomal microscleres consist of microspinose spiraster streptasters with slender arms. There are bundles of smooth very long oxeas in long thick brushes piercing the surface.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2252103",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "2c079f81-b7ff-5cc-ba2-2aeffa1db0a2c1",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "3Q2PY"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:3Q2PY"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ISABELLA_TANOA_EKINS_ERPENBECK_W_RHEIDE_HOOPER_2016",
          "name": "Isabella tanoa Ekins, Erpenbeck, Wörheide & Hooper, 2016",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Isabella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Isabella mirabilis also has smooth centrotylote microxeas. The microspined microxeas in I. tanoa are generally more slender than those in I. mirabilis and I. harborbranchi. I. tanoa lacks the fusiform microacanthoxeas found in I. mirabilis and I. harborbranchi and the long thin blunt oxeas found in I. harborbranchi. Isabella tanoa and I. mirabilis both have extremely long and slightly curved oxeas. However they are longer and thicker in I. tanoa. Both I. tanoa and I. mirabilis species have long oxeas, which pierce the surface in brushes, extending several millimetres above the sponge surface. Isabella tanoa does not have either of the shorter oxeas found in I. harborbranchi. Isabella tanoa lacks the long and short-shafted triaenes present in I. mirabilis and I. harborbranchi. Isabella tanoa has short-shafted dichotriaenes with rounded rhabdome tips, that are also present in I. mirabilis, however the dichotriaenes in I. tanoa are delicate and slender and only half the width of the stouter I. mirabilis dichotriaenes. All three species have similar large spirasters with long thin arms. Isabella mirabilis contain thick streptasters ‘ Jacks’ that do not occur in either I. tanoa or I. harborbranchi. However, only I. tanoa and I. harborbranchi have the long spirasters with short thick thorny arms. Isabella tanoa has a combination of both graceful desmas in the subectosome region and the interlocking desmas as in I. mirabilis in the choanosomal skeleton. Both I. tanoa and I.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:8473925",
          "authorship": "Ekins, Erpenbeck, Wörheide & Hooper",
          "yearPublished": "2016",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "244437fb-f780-5ce-8e1-02984b59a9c588",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "3Q2PZ"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:3Q2PZ"
        }
      ]
